>   // "Initial" (01) is the minimal enable the abstract FPR writes require.
>   explicit ResumeDriver(DmiBus& bus) : bus_{bus} {}
>     // mstatus: enable FS so the following FPR abstract writes are accepted
>     // (FS == Off disables the extension and the hart NACKs the writes). The
>     // drained state.mstatus may legitimately carry FS at Off (e.g. an OS
>     // context-switched the regs away before the trigger fired) -- gating the
>     // write on the drained field skips the enable and silently NACKs every
>     // subsequent FPR write. Always write mstatus when FP is in scope;
>     // force-OR Initial when the drained field is Off. This enable is local
>     // to the vsim phase; the state.mstatus written to the handoff file is
>     // left unmodified.
